WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.624
Here's the same easel stand you drew by hand, built in Onshape. This is a preview: you start Onshape next week.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:17.857
Your drawing shows the stand from the side. In Onshape, we sketch that same side view: lip, ledge, back, and brace.

00:00:18.407 --> 00:00:27.219
Then we add the same dimensions you wrote on paper: a 0.4 in lip, a 0.8 in ledge, and a 3.2 in back.

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:35.037
The back leans at 105°. With every size set, the lines turn black. That means fully defined.

00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:43.621
The sheet metal tool turns the side view into folded cardboard: 1.2 in wide and 0.02 in thick.

00:00:44.171 --> 00:00:50.266
Here's the folded stand. Same part, two ways to describe it: your drawing and the model.

00:00:50.816 --> 00:01:00.069
Onshape can also unfold it. This flat strip is what the laser cuts. Each bend becomes a scored line, so it folds cleanly.
